= Spurious correlation — Technical =

== Environment dependence ==
Let feature Z correlate with target Y in source environment e_s:

<pre>
Corr_e_s(Z,Y) ≠ 0
</pre>

but weaken/reverse across target environments.

A learner minimizing source risk can exploit Z even if Z is unstable relative to the intended task mechanism.

== Sources ==
Spurious association can arise from confounding, collider/selection bias, measurement policy, class imbalance, background context, or collection procedures.

The term should therefore not be reduced to one causal graph pattern.

== Robustness ==
Methods for mitigating spurious features include group-aware objectives, environment variation, causal/invariant approaches, data augmentation, reweighting, representation constraints, and targeted evaluation.

No method is universally reliable.

